	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Keystone CAT 3557 UNIVERSAL CLIP, Top Entry -- bare brass auto-blade-fuse clip, tin-nickel plate, UL 30A @ 500V AC, THT ('maintains position during wave soldering'), catalog M55 p.41 (lib/datasheets/Keystone_3557-2.pdf -- NAMING NOTE: that vendored PDF page carries BOTH products; '3557-2' is the 2-IN-1 HOUSED FUSE HOLDER, a different line item; THIS part is the bare single clip). Body .150x.185x.400in (3.8 x 4.7 x 10.2mm tall); jaw .062/.027 (1.57/0.69); 2 legs .063 (1.60) dia at .134 (3.4mm) centres. LEG-PAIR AXIS, verified against the mounting details: the legs run PERPENDICULAR to the jaw/slot axis (the 3557-2 housed detail shows per-clip 3.4mm leg pairs perpendicular to the 13.5mm fuse axis, and an ATO blade's 5.2mm width runs ALONG the fuse axis: 13.5+5.2 = the fuse's ~18.7mm width -- so slot IS parallel to the fuse axis, legs perpendicular). Local frame = the CEC main-board mating orientation (blade-fit memo addendum 5): slot axis along +Y (perpendicular to the daughterboard wall line, accepting the descending 63951-1 blade broadside); legs at (+/-1.7, 0) ALONG the row (X); body 3.8 (X) x 4.7 (Y), legs' outer extent 5.0 along X (feet splay past the body sides). Drill 1.60 = the leg dia (friction fit for wave solder, same 1.6mm figure the fit memo Sec.6 corrected the 3557-2 holes to); pad 2.4mm (0.4 annulus -- the joint current rides the surrounding pour, keep NO thermal relief per the memo Sec.5). Along-row pad span 3.4+2.4 = 5.8mm -- THE row-pitch floor driver (5.8 + 0.5 solder web = 6.3mm), see the daughterboard TAB_PITCH derivation. Jaw designed for .025in/0.64mm fuse blades; the platform's 63951-1 tab is 0.77-0.83mm -- inside the family's published .020-.032 acceptance but 27% over the fuse design-centre = stiffer grip, the memo addendum-5 #1 sample-gate item.")
